---
title: Spaghetti Carbonara
description: No cream.
category: Mains
tags:
  - Italian
  - quick
  - pasta
servings: 4
image: /src/assets/recipes/mains/spaghetti-carbonara.jpg
prep time: 10 minutes
cook time: 20 minutes
created: 2026-05-17
updated: 2026-05-17
---

Bring a large pot of salted water to a boil. Cook @spaghetti{400%g} until al dente, about ~{10%minutes}. Reserve @pasta water{} before draining.

While the water boils, toast @black pepper{} in a skillet for ~{2%minutes} and set aside.

Cut @guanciale{200%g} into lardons and cook in a cold #skillet{} over medium heat until the fat renders and the meat is crispy, about ~{8%minutes}. Remove from heat.

In a bowl, whisk together @egg{1} and @egg yolks{4} and @pecorino romano{80%g}(finely grated).

Add the drained pasta to the skillet with the guanciale. Turn off the heat and pour in the egg mixture and toss rapidly, adding pasta water a splash at a time until the sauce is glossy and coats every strand.

Crush the black pepper grounds and season generously. Serve immediately.
